==============================================================================
- "Author" refers to the copyright holder and creator of the Software (smin987).
- "Software" refers collectively to zipper9, including all source code,
  documentation, assets, scripts, and compiled executable binaries.
- "Source Code" refers to the human-readable programming language instructions,
  scripts, build recipes, and project assets making up the Software.
- "Compiled Binaries" refers to the machine-executable files, packages, and
  installers (including Windows .exe, macOS .dmg/.app, and Linux binaries/.deb)
  officially compiled and published by the Author.
- "Competing Product" refers to any software, application, library, service, or
  derivative work that provides similar core archive compression, decompression,
  or archival management functionality and is distributed to third parties.
- "Commercial Entity" refers to any for-profit corporation, company, partnership,
